# ============================================================
#  The four-year loop's fixed beats (design §4, §7; phase 2b).
#  These replace the old calendar menus and exams, which are
#  retired by tools/migrations/0001-retire-v02-calendar.js.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Enrolment (design §7.3): two courses a term ----------------

@event enrolment
title: Enrolment
trigger: auto
when: term and (month == 1 or month == 7)
repeat: 6
priority: 80
type: menu
offers: courses
pick: 2
class: story
tone: light
art: scroll
tags: class study
scene: The registrar's hall at the start of term, students queueing at long tables with course lists that rewrite themselves.
text: {term_index == 1: Your first term. The registrar slides a list across the desk: four courses open to first-years.|A new term, and a new list. Courses you've passed are gone from it; new levels have appeared.} Choose two. Course fees are eight crowns.
on_show:
  gold -small
> none: Take no courses this term
  hint: Allowed. Your GPA will not thank you.
  mood +small
  say: You hand back the list blank. The registrar raises one eyebrow, which is the whole of her opinion.

# ---------------- Club Fair (design §7.4): one club at a time ----------------

@event club_fair_v3
title: The Club Fair
trigger: auto
when: month == 2
repeat: 12
priority: 60
type: menu
offers: clubs
class: story
tone: light
art: group
tags: club festival
scene: The courtyard full of recruiting tables, banners snapping, a duelling demonstration drawing a crowd.
text: The Club Fair fills the courtyard. Every table wants you; every captain swears theirs is the one that matters. {rel(lyra) >= 6: Lyra is at the Duelling Circle's table, pretending not to watch which way you walk.|}
> none: Not this year
  hint: You can join at next year's fair.
  mood +tiny
  say: You collect three leaflets and a free biscuit, and sign nothing.

# ---------------- The Job Board (design §7.4): visiting it is the change event ----------------

@event job_board_visit
title: The Job Board
place: job_board
repeat: 1
weight: 30
type: menu
offers: jobs
class: story
tone: light
art: paper
tags: job money
scene: A cork board crowded with notices, a student running a finger down a column of shift times.
text: Notices for work, three layers deep: the library, the Gilded Newt, Pell & Daughters, the courier loft. Each wants someone reliable. Each says so twice.
> look: Just looking
  mood +tiny
  say: You read every notice twice and take none of them down.
> quit: Hand in your notice
  when: member(library_assistant) or member(tavern) or member(apothecary_clerk) or member(broom_courier)
  hint: You can find work again later.
  leave job
  mood +small
  say: You hand in your notice. Your evenings are yours again; so is your empty purse.

# ---------------- Break plans (design §4.3) ----------------

@event break_plan
title: The Break
trigger: auto
when: break and (month == 5 or month == 11) and not wrapup
repeat: 6
priority: 75
type: menu
class: story
tone: warm
art: sun
tags: home
scene: The academy gates thrown open, barges loading trunks, a few students lingering on the steps with nowhere they'd rather be.
text: {month == 5: The winter break.|The summer break.} Two months without lectures. The castle empties, mostly.
> castle: Stay at the castle
  hint: Quiet corridors and secrets. Board 8 crowns a month.
  gain plan_castle
  say: The castle in the holidays is a different building: louder echoes, kinder staff, doors you've never seen open.
> home: Go home
  hint: Family, old friends, free board.
  gain plan_home
  say: The barge, the coach, the last mile on foot. Home is smaller than you remember, and warmer.
> work: Work full-time
  when: member(library_assistant) or member(tavern) or member(apothecary_clerk) or member(broom_courier)
  hint: Extra shifts at double pay.
  gain plan_work
  say: You trade the holidays for wages. Your feet will remember it.
> intern: Start your internship
  when: member(intern_royal_library) or member(intern_conclave) or member(intern_alchemists) or member(intern_expedition) or member(intern_field_station) or member(intern_thornwick) or member(intern_unseen_office)
  hint: A stipend, a supervisor and a project.
  gain plan_internship
  say: You pack a trunk of notebooks and take the long coach to the capital.

# ---------------- Track notices (pushed by the engine at term end) ----------------

@event course_exam
title: Exam Day
trigger: queued
class: story
tone: tense
art: scroll
tags: study class
scene: A silent exam hall in late light, rows of bent heads, an hourglass on the invigilator's desk.
text: Exam day for {track}. The hall is silent except for quills and somebody's knee bouncing under a desk. {~The paper is long.|The first question is one you revised.|The first question is one you didn't.|The invigilator turns the hourglass with a click you feel in your teeth.}
> left: Answer what you know, carefully
  sit_exam steady
  say: {~You write slowly: everything you're sure of, and nothing you aren't.|You check every answer twice and hand in at the bell.}
> right: Go for top marks
  sit_exam wild
  say: {~You take the hardest question first and gamble the essay on an idea you had at breakfast.|You write the answer you'd want to read, not the safe one.}

@event track_warning
title: A Word About Your Attendance
trigger: queued
class: incident
tone: tense
art: paper
tags: job club
scene: A folded note on official paper, the words "performance" and "concern" underlined twice.
text: A note about {track}: your attendance and your efforts have slipped, and it has been noticed. One more term like this and there will be consequences.
> left: Promise to do better
  mood -small
  say: You write back a promise in your neatest hand. Now you'll have to keep it.
> right: Let it slide
  perform track -small
  mood +tiny
  say: You put the note in a drawer. It doesn't stop existing in the drawer.

@event track_promotion
title: A Step Up
trigger: queued
class: milestone
tone: warm
art: trophy
tags: job club
scene: A small ceremony in a cramped room, someone pinning a badge to a student's collar while the others applaud.
text: {track} wants to promote you. More responsibility, more respect, and in the right places, more pay.
> left: Accept
  promote track
  renown +small
  mood +small
  say: The badge is a little crooked. You don't straighten it.
> right: Not yet
  mood +tiny
  say: "When you're ready, then." They mean it. The offer will come again.

# ---------------- Research internship (design §7.5; the Royal Library is the slice host) ----------------

@event intern_application
title: Applications Open
trigger: auto
repeat: 2
priority: 50
type: menu
when: month == 7 and year >= 2 and year <= 3 and not (applied(intern_royal_library) or applied(intern_conclave) or applied(intern_alchemists) or applied(intern_expedition) or applied(intern_field_station) or applied(intern_thornwick))
class: story
tone: light
art: letter
tags: job study
scene: A cluster of notices with wax seals pinned above all the others: summer research posts, each with its own demands.
text: Summer research posts are open. Six notices, six seals, six lists of requirements. You can put your name to one this year.
> royal: The Royal Library
  when: not member(intern_royal_library)
  hint: GPA 2.5, Astromancy II, a love of indexes.
  apply intern_royal_library
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> conclave: The Conclave Laboratory
  when: not member(intern_conclave)
  hint: GPA 3.0, Evocation II, and a word from Thorne.
  apply intern_conclave
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> alchemists: The Guild of Alchemists' Works
  when: not member(intern_alchemists)
  hint: GPA 2.0, Alchemy II, a strong stomach.
  apply intern_alchemists
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> expedition: The Observatory Expedition
  when: not member(intern_expedition)
  hint: Astromancy II and the legs for a plateau.
  apply intern_expedition
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> field: The Beastcraft Field Station
  when: not member(intern_field_station)
  hint: Beastcraft II. Boots provided, mostly.
  apply intern_field_station
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> thornwick: The Thornwick Exchange
  when: not member(intern_thornwick)
  hint: GPA 2.5 and Illusion II. Bring a thick skin.
  apply intern_thornwick
  charm +tiny
  say: You write the letter three times and send the best one. Probably the best one.
> none: Not this year
  mood -tiny
  say: You let the notices flap. There's always next year, until there isn't.

@event intern_offer
title: Letters With Seals
trigger: auto
type: menu
when: month == 9 and year >= 2 and year <= 3 and (applied(intern_royal_library) or applied(intern_conclave) or applied(intern_alchemists) or applied(intern_expedition) or applied(intern_field_station) or applied(intern_thornwick) or (guile >= 35 and rel(isolde) >= 6 and not member(intern_unseen_office)))
repeat: 12
priority: 55
class: milestone
tone: warm
art: letter
tags: study
scene: Heavy envelopes with wax seals on a dormitory desk, one of them plain grey with no seal at all.
text: The spring post brings answers. {(applied(intern_royal_library) and gpa >= 2.5 and level(astromancy) >= 2) or (applied(intern_conclave) and gpa >= 3.0 and level(evocation) >= 2 and rel(thorne) >= 6) or (applied(intern_alchemists) and gpa >= 2.0 and level(alchemy) >= 2) or (applied(intern_expedition) and level(astromancy) >= 2 and vigor >= 20) or (applied(intern_field_station) and level(beastcraft) >= 2) or (applied(intern_thornwick) and gpa >= 2.5 and level(illusion) >= 2): One of them begins "We are pleased".|Every letter begins with "We regret".} {guile >= 35 and rel(isolde) >= 6: There is also a plain grey envelope you never asked for.|}
> royal: Accept: The Royal Library
  when: applied(intern_royal_library) and gpa >= 2.5 and level(astromancy) >= 2
  join intern_royal_library
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the oldest archives in the realm.
> conclave: Accept: The Conclave Laboratory
  when: applied(intern_conclave) and gpa >= 3.0 and level(evocation) >= 2 and rel(thorne) >= 6
  join intern_conclave
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in spell research under the Seven Towers.
> alchemists: Accept: The Alchemists' Works
  when: applied(intern_alchemists) and gpa >= 2.0 and level(alchemy) >= 2
  join intern_alchemists
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the great vats of the Guild.
> expedition: Accept: The Observatory Expedition
  when: applied(intern_expedition) and level(astromancy) >= 2 and vigor >= 20
  join intern_expedition
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer of sky charts on the high plateau.
> field: Accept: The Beastcraft Field Station
  when: applied(intern_field_station) and level(beastcraft) >= 2
  join intern_field_station
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the moors, the heather and the creatures in them.
> thornwick: Accept: The Thornwick Exchange
  when: applied(intern_thornwick) and gpa >= 2.5 and level(illusion) >= 2
  join intern_thornwick
  renown +small
  say: You read the letter until the seal cracks. A summer in the rival academy's illusion laboratory.
> unseen: Open the plain envelope
  when: guile >= 35 and rel(isolde) >= 6 and not member(intern_unseen_office)
  join intern_unseen_office
  guile +small
  say: Inside: a time, an address and no signature. The paper is blank again by morning. You go anyway.
> decline: Fold the letters away
  leave intern_royal_library
  leave intern_conclave
  leave intern_alchemists
  leave intern_expedition
  leave intern_field_station
  leave intern_thornwick
  mood -tiny
  say: You fold them carefully. Next year, perhaps.

# ---------------- Thesis (design §7.6) ----------------

@event thesis_setup
title: Choosing a Thesis
trigger: auto
when: year == 4 and month == 1 and not member(thesis)
repeat: 12
priority: 85
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
art: book
tags: study
scene: A professor's study, three topic proposals laid out on the desk like cards.
text: The final year opens with a thesis. Before you choose this term's courses, Professor Thorne lays out three topics, at three levels of ambition.
> safe: A careful survey
  hint: Easier, and it will read as easier.
  join thesis
  flag thesis_safe
  say: A sensible topic. Thorne says "Sensible," the way other people say "Disappointing."
> solid: An original study
  hint: The usual path.
  join thesis
  flag thesis_solid
  say: Thorne nods. "Good. Bring me something I don't already know."
> ambitious: Something no one has done
  hint: Harder, and worth more.
  join thesis
  flag thesis_ambitious
  say: Thorne is quiet for a long time. "Hm," he says, and for once it sounds like hope.

@event thesis_crunch
title: The Crunch
trigger: auto
when: final_year and month == 9 and member(thesis) and progress(thesis) < 60
repeat: 12
priority: 40
class: incident
tone: tense
art: hourglass
tags: study
scene: A thesis carrel at dawn, a candle burned to a stub, drafts on the floor and a student asleep on the keyboard of a typing-quill.
text: The defence is next month and your thesis is not ready. Your advisor's note is three words long: "Well? Final draft."
> left: Work through the nights
  progress thesis +large
  health -medium
  mood -medium
  say: You stop seeing daylight. The draft gets better and you get worse, which seems to be how this works.
> right: Hand in what you have
  mood +tiny
  progress thesis +small
  say: You tidy what's there and accept the gaps. Your advisor sighs, which is not the same as no.

@event thesis_defence
title: The Defence
trigger: auto
when: final_year and month == 10 and member(thesis)
repeat: 12
priority: 65
class: story
tone: tense
art: scroll
tags: study exam
scene: A semicircular table with three examiners, a student standing at a lectern with a stack of notes.
text: Three examiners, one lectern, and a year of work. {progress(thesis) >= 60: You know this material better than anyone in the room.|There are gaps, and you know where they are.}
> left: Defend it
  hint: A safe topic is easier to defend and earns less; an ambitious one is harder and earns more.
  if not (flag(thesis_safe) or flag(thesis_ambitious)):
    challenge negotiate using lore hard:
      win:
        flag thesis_distinction
        renown +large
        say: They stop asking questions and start asking for copies. Distinction.
      partial:
        flag thesis_passed
        renown +small
        say: A pass, with one examiner's handwriting all over your conclusion.
      lose:
        flag thesis_resubmit
        mood -large
        say: They send you away to resubmit. It isn't the end. It feels like it.
  elif flag(thesis_safe):
    challenge negotiate using lore medium:
      win:
        flag thesis_distinction
        renown +medium
        say: A careful survey, carefully defended. They give you a distinction and the faint air of people who wished you'd risked more.
      partial:
        flag thesis_passed
        renown +tiny
        say: A pass. Nobody argues with a careful survey. Nobody remembers it either.
      lose:
        flag thesis_resubmit
        mood -medium
        say: Even a safe topic has its gaps, and they find every one. Resubmit.
  else:
    challenge negotiate using lore heroic:
      win:
        flag thesis_distinction
        renown +huge
        if clue(seven_locks) + clue(star_key) + clue(ilse_truth) >= 3:
          flag thesis_hollowstar
        say: Something no one has done, and now someone has. The committee stands when you finish. One of them is crying, and pretending not to.
      partial:
        flag thesis_passed
        renown +medium
        say: They pass it, arguing among themselves about whether it is brilliant or mad. Possibly both.
      lose:
        flag thesis_resubmit
        mood -large
        renown -small
        say: You reached too far, and they tell you so, at length. Resubmit. The idea was good. The proof wasn't there yet.
  # The defence closes the thesis: its lab events stop (B30).
  leave thesis

# ---------------- Festivals that take a visit (design §4.4) ----------------

@event lantern_night_v3
title: Lantern Night
place: lakeshore
replaces: visit2
when: month == 2
repeat: 12
class: milestone
tone: warm
art: lantern
tags: festival
scene: The Mirror Lake at night, hundreds of paper lanterns drifting over the water, students crowding the shore.
text: Lantern Night. The whole academy gathers on the lakeshore with paper lanterns, each carrying a wish out over the water. {month == 2 and year == 1: Your first one.|Another year, another wish.}
> left: Wish for something selfish
  mood +medium
  renown +tiny
  say: Your lantern goes out over the water and keeps its secret. You feel lighter for having asked.
> right: Wish for someone else
  mood +small
  alignment +small
  say: You don't tell anyone who. The lantern seems to know; it flies straight.

# ---------------- Calendar beats ----------------

@event year_four
title: The Final Year
trigger: auto
when: turn == 37
priority: 90
class: story
tone: warm
art: tower
tags: story
scene: The seven towers at dawn from the barge, the same view as the first day, but the student watching it has changed.
text: The barge again, the towers again, and a thesis waiting. The first-years on the deck look at you the way you once looked at the fourth-years. At the opening feast the headmistress says, "Fourth years, this is your last year in these halls. What you become here, you will be for a long time." She looks, for a moment, directly at you.
> ok: Here we go
  mood +small
  say: You know which steps creak. You know which doors stick. One more year to learn the rest.
